WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.350
When time travel gets involved there isn't
much that isn't possible, and with so many

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.810
possibilities on the table it's easy to choke
the air with questions.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:14.630
In the aftermath of Terminator: Dark Fate,
this franchise has as many dangling plot threads

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:15.650
as ever.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:20.320
Sadly, we learn early in Terminator: Dark
Fate that John Connor is no longer in the

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.750
land of the living.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:27.380
Even though the only bad guy Terminator we
meet in Terminator 2 is Robert Patrick's T-1000,

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.820
in Dark Fate we learn SkyNet covered all of
its angles and sent more Terminators back

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.100
in time that we didn't know about.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.040
After the events of Terminator 2, one of those
Terminators, the same model as the classic

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.970
Schwarzenegger cyborg we're used to, kills
John Connor in front of Sarah.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:49.309
With SkyNet no longer in existence, the Terminator
receives no new orders and decides to learn

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:53.110
to become more human, eventually regretting
his actions.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:58.289
It begs the question of why SkyNet sends this
older Terminator model as a safety net when

00:00:58.289 --> 00:01:03.130
the T-1000 version we see in Terminator 2
is clearly superior and can take a lot more

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.130
punishment.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:08.310
The real answer is obvious, because Arnold
didn't play the T-1000, and the filmmakers

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:09.850
wanted Arnold back.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:13.659
But narratively we don't get any kind of explanation.

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:15.850
Maybe T-1000s were rare?

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:21.369
Perhaps one T-1000 per time travel kill mission
was the limit in SkyNet Central?

00:01:21.369 --> 00:01:23.250
We'll probably never know.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:28.509
When Sarah Connor explains that the T-1000
wasn't the only Terminator SkyNet sent back

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:33.919
during the events of Terminator 2, she doesn't
specify that the one who kills John is the

00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:36.009
only other Terminator.

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:40.899
Since Carl is still around in a world without
Skynet, it's possible that there are other

00:01:40.899 --> 00:01:43.990
Skynet models that were sent back in time.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:48.469
Could there be more Schwarzenegger cyborgs
out there, growing old in cabins in the woods

00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:50.039
and working modest jobs?

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:54.989
Maybe a Terminator who sells vacuum cleaners,
or an Uber driver?

00:01:54.989 --> 00:01:57.349
"Give you a lift?"

00:01:57.349 --> 00:02:02.130
It leaves possibilities open for future Terminator
installments, particularly if they want to

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.740
bring Schwarzenegger back.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:08.569
Sure, his death looks pretty final at the
end of Dark Fate...exactly like it does at

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:13.500
the end of Terminator...and the end of Terminator
2.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:18.739
Once Grace accepts Sarah Connor into the fold,
Connor explains that for years she's been

00:02:18.739 --> 00:02:23.150
receiving texts with coordinates from an anonymous
source.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:27.569
Once she goes to the coordinates to investigate,
she finds a Terminator waiting for her.

00:02:27.569 --> 00:02:31.569
We don't know exactly how many times Sarah's
done this, though it seems she's killed at

00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:34.189
least two or three Terminators offscreen.

00:02:34.189 --> 00:02:38.159
The question is, why were those Terminators
sent back?

00:02:38.159 --> 00:02:39.159
What were their missions?

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.790
"Who sent him back?"

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.569
"Those files have been erased."

00:02:42.569 --> 00:02:44.150
"Oh that's convenient."

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:49.330
Since SkyNet is gone, they must have been
Legion-controlled Terminators, so were they

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:52.680
all supposed to kill Dani before Sarah killed
them?

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.250
If so, that would seem strange.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:59.799
We're given the impression Dani has spent
most, if not all, of her life in Mexico up

00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:03.700
to this point, meaning any Terminators sent
to kill her would show up there.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.579
And if all of the Terminators Sarah hunted
down popped up in Mexico, you'd also think

00:03:08.579 --> 00:03:13.999
she might wonder why and maybe investigate
exactly who the cyborgs were looking for.

00:03:13.999 --> 00:03:18.060
Since Sarah doesn't seem to have any idea
who Dani is before she saves her from the

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:26.120
Rev-9 Terminator, it's likely Dani hasn't
been Legion's only target over the years.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.950
Let's talk about Carl's family.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.790
Do they really not know he's a cyborg?

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.849
Carl explains to Sarah that his relationship
with his wife isn't physical.

00:03:34.849 --> 00:03:40.120
Still, the boy he's helped raise since infancy
is a teenager, meaning Carl's been with his

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.659
wife for over a decade.

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:46.470
You don't live with someone for that long
and fail to notice their physical "quirks."

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:49.370
It's not impossible, but it's a tough sell.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.040
There are a couple of other things.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:56.349
First, when Carl tells his wife and child
to leave home and that he won't be back, they

00:03:56.349 --> 00:03:57.760
don't make a lot of fuss.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:02.129
You would think a family might have a few
discussions before agreeing to completely

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:03.359
split forever.

00:04:03.359 --> 00:04:05.790
Second, the family has a dog.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:10.849
Anyone who's seen 1984's Terminator knows
that dogs don't like Terminators.

00:04:10.849 --> 00:04:15.260
It's why human communities in the future keep
dogs at their entrances, and why at the end

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:19.229
of the film Sarah Connor has a new dog in
her jeep.

00:04:19.229 --> 00:04:23.930
How is this dog hanging out with Carl without
constantly freaking out?

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:29.919
At first Sarah Connor assumes that, like in
her case in 1984's Terminator, Dani's unborn

00:04:29.919 --> 00:04:32.949
child is the key to defeating Legion.

00:04:32.949 --> 00:04:37.510
Once we find out it's Dani herself that Grace
is desperate to protect, you might wonder

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:42.479
how much the Dani of the future has seen of
the events of Terminator: Dark Fate.

00:04:42.479 --> 00:04:48.280
Are Grace, Sarah, Dani, and Carl succeeding
in creating a new future, or has the Dani

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.930
of the future seen all of it before?

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:55.569
When we meet the older, more battle-hardened
Dani, does she know the young girl she saves

00:04:55.569 --> 00:04:59.500
from scavengers is destined to sacrifice herself
for her?

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:04.940
She seems to be a little affected by learning
Grace's name, so that could be the case.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:09.690
But there are some reasons to believe the
heroes are genuinely changing things.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:15.470
The future Dani tells Grace not to tell her
younger self that she'll grow to become humanity's

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:19.110
unifying figure, yet Grace does reveal it.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:24.199
So why would Dani bother giving her that advice
if she already knows Grace is going to ignore

00:05:24.199 --> 00:05:25.229
it?

00:05:25.229 --> 00:05:29.750
One of the most inexplicable things that happens
in Terminator: Dark Fate is that the heroes

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:34.560
get a very unlikely ally, the U.S. military.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:39.680
Deciding they'll need an EMP weapon to fry
the Rev-9 Terminator's systems, Sarah gets

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:45.210
in touch with Major Dean, who says he's committing
treason by stealing the item for Sarah.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:50.760
The Rev-9 attacks during the handoff and the
heroes escape to a nearby military airfield.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:55.199
All on Major Dean's say-so, the heroes meet
no military resistance and are allowed to

00:05:55.199 --> 00:06:00.759
abruptly commandeer a C-5 Galaxy transport
aircraft and receive a fighter escort in the

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:01.930
air.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:04.930
Just who is Major Dean that he can get them
all of this?

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:09.610
From Terminator 2 we know that, offscreen,
Sarah had brief relationships with lots of

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:14.240
military "types," but the impression given
is that none of them were high-ranking military

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.270
officers.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:20.569
The idea that this rag-tag crew of cyborgs
and wanted criminals could peacefully commandeer

00:06:20.569 --> 00:06:27.229
a military aircraft suggests one of two things:
some lazy storytelling, or in the world of

00:06:27.229 --> 00:06:31.090
Terminator the U.S. government knows more
about these time-jumping cyborgs than they're

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.750
letting on.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:36.909
Maybe certain officers like Major Dean are
tasked with giving people like Sarah Connor

00:06:36.909 --> 00:06:43.280
off-the-books support if the opportunity arises.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:48.349
In Dark Fate we learn that while Sarah Connor
and the other heroes of Terminator 2 succeeded

00:06:48.349 --> 00:06:54.819
in ridding the future of SkyNet, another artificial
intelligence, this time a cyberwarfare AI

00:06:54.819 --> 00:06:58.759
called Legion, is what spells doom for civilization.

00:06:58.759 --> 00:07:03.930
There is one question left unanswered, though
to be fair, the same question is left unanswered

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:06.160
in the other Terminator films.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.440
Specifically: Why?

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:13.800
Why is it that as soon as these powerful new
forms of artificial intelligence go online,

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:17.510
their first thought is to eradicate or subjugate
humanity?

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:22.659
Do these AIs simply see us as inferior beings
who are wrecking a planet they could be better

00:07:22.659 --> 00:07:24.129
caretakers for?

00:07:24.129 --> 00:07:29.580
Do they see us as a threat and figure that
killing us all is the best safeguard?

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:33.110
Any of the answers could work, but we've yet
to hear them.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:37.710
All we know is that apparently when computers
become self-aware, they immediately want to

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:39.330
kill everybody.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.580
Maybe it's all the memes we made them endure?

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:44.199
"Computer, load up celery man please."

00:07:44.199 --> 00:07:46.930
"Yes, Paul."

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:49.659
Who knows!

00:07:49.659 --> 00:07:57.860
Terminator: Dark Fate ends with three dead
cyborgs, The Rev-9, the T-800, and Grace.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:03.020
What should not escape the notice of any Terminator
fan is while the Rev-9 body seems pretty well

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:08.780
slagged, Grace's body and the T-800 are more
or less intact and we never get any indication

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.710
that the bodies are destroyed.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:15.840
It could be that Sarah and Dani destroyed
the corpses offscreen, but if not, there's

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:21.039
a chance Sarah forgot a very important lesson
from the first two Terminator movies.

00:08:21.039 --> 00:08:26.090
In Terminator 2: Judgment Day, we learn it
was largely because of the body of the T-800

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:30.110
Sarah Connor kills in Terminator that SkyNet
was being developed.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:35.570
At the end of that film, the T-800 who protects
John Connor chooses to descend into molten

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:37.970
liquid, destroying his body.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:43.190
Unless there's a body disposal scene we don't
see, Terminator: Dark Fate ends with the bodies

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:48.330
of several cyborgs for someone to pick apart,
reverse engineer, and create Legion or an

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.100
AI just as bad.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:55.380
In fact, even if the bodies were destroyed
off-screen, there are still the scans of Grace's

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:59.690
body taken while she was in Border Patrol
custody.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:03.510
This is a question that someone should have
asked a long time ago.

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:09.870
In Terminator, the super-intelligent AI SkyNet
sends a single T-800 Terminator back in time

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.770
to kill the mother of John Connor.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:14.000
It almost succeeds.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:19.890
In Terminator 2: Judgment Day, the same AI
sends a new and improved liquid metal cyborg,

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:23.400
the T-1000, back in time to kill John Connor.

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:28.100
In spite of a T-800 sent by the humans to
protect John and the fact that Sarah Connor

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:34.080
is trained, heavily armed, and expecting an
attack from the future, the T-1000 almost

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.080
succeeds.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:40.920
And now, in Terminator: Dark Fate, the new
super-intelligent AI Legion sends a single

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:44.910
Rev-9 Terminator back in time to kill Dani
Ramos.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:49.630
Dani has backup from a cybernetically augmented
human soldier, another T-800 Terminator, and

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:55.570
an even more heavily armed Sarah Connor, and
still the Rev-9 almost succeeds.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:10:02.440
Do you think...you know...one of those obscenely
intelligent AI world-killers might just splurge

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:05.380
and send back, maybe...two Terminators?

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:11.310
Sure, we find out SkyNet did just that, but
the Terminators SkyNet sent back weren't working

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:12.310
together.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:17.720
If one Terminator, completely on its own,
almost does the job, why not send back partners?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.470
What's the big deal?

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:20.470
Maybe even a three-fer?

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.470
Four?

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.170
Make a party of it.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:29.690
"Well isn't this cute...a Terminator convention."

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:34.170
Everything about the journey of Carl feels
like the end of Arnold Schwarzenegger's involvement

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.290
with the Terminator franchise.

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:40.730
Just as the earlier model does at the end
of Terminator 3, Carl sacrifices himself to

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:43.340
make sure the Rev-9 is down for the count.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:48.260
When he talks about telling his family that
he "won't be back," if feels like he's telling

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:50.090
us the same thing.

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:55.070
Also, Schwarzenegger's in his 70s, and his
best killer android days are arguably behind

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:56.070
him.

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.280
But you never know.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:01.290
Terminator: Dark Fate leaves the door open
for Schwarzenegger's return.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:06.150
In Dark Fate we learn that during the events
of Terminator 2, SkyNet sent at least one

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:11.450
other Terminator to 1991; there's no reason
it couldn't have sent others.

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:16.710
Not to mention that from the texts Carl sends
Sarah over the years to warn her of Terminator

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:21.360
infiltration, Legion was sending more cyborgs
to the present day.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:25.410
There's no way to know for sure if Sarah got
them all.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:28.750
Schwarzenegger's not getting any younger,
but he can probably keep fighting cyborgs

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.470
for a couple more years if he wants.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:32.980
Dude's still in great shape.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:37.170
"Come with me if you want to lift."

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:42.030
There's probably a good chance that this really
is the end for Linda Hamilton's involvement

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.350
in the Terminator franchise.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:49.070
Hamilton apparently didn't even initially
want to come back for Terminator: Dark Fate.

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:53.660
In an interview about the movie, Hamilton
seemed less than eager to return to the franchise,

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:54.660
quipping,

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:58.710
"I've been threatening to fake my own death
so I wouldn't have to do the next one if there

00:11:58.710 --> 00:11:59.710
is one."

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:03.820
Ironically, while it does seem more likely
we'll see Schwarzenegger than it does we'll

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:08.060
see Hamilton, it's Sarah Connor's story that's
left with more potential.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:13.330
By the end of Dark Fate Connor seems to have
found whatever peace she's likely to find

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:18.560
over the death of her son, so in that sense
you could argue her story is over.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:23.890
But Dani Ramos still has a big fight to prepare
for, and Sarah Connor is her only surviving

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:24.890
ally.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:30.180
As a bonafide badass Terminator hunter who's
been killing time-hopping cyborgs for decades,

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:34.611
Sarah Connor is the best mentor the future
savior of humanity could ask for.

00:12:34.611 --> 00:12:35.611
"Enough of a resume for you?"

